    <item>
      <title>Anything Not Saved Will Be Lost | Acta Victoriana</title>
      <link>https://actavictoriana.ca/culture/anything-not-saved-will-be-lost/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=anything-not-saved-will-be-lost</link>
      <description>This kind of place feels almost inevitable, doesn’t it? After all, what could be more natural than this pursuit, than to try and catch memories falling from the sky? We clutch at nostalgia, tie it to technology, let our yearning find purchase on wires and bytes. It doesn’t matter that each piece of data is as mortal as we are.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://actavictoriana.ca/culture/anything-not-saved-will-be-lost/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=anything-not-saved-will-be-lost</guid>
